cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these data, please cite the associated article."
title: "certus_re"
abstract: >-
  Reverse engineering of multilayer optical coatings from measured reflectance and
  transmittance spectra. Several samples are inverted jointly, sharing the coatings they
  have in common; two-side-coated components are handled with a coherent stack on each face
  and the substrate treated incoherently between them; the finite beam aperture is modelled
  as a piecewise-constant function of wavelength, stepped at the instrument's documented
  source and detector switchovers; the imperfect extinction of the polarizer is modelled as
  a leakage of each polarization channel into the other, with one pair of coefficients for
  the whole instrument. Every run declares, counts and reports the parameter blocks it is
  allowed to move, and quotes the uncertainty the data imply on every retrieved quarter
  wave, so that a residual can be read next to the number of degrees of freedom that
  produced it. Includes the measured spectra of a six-layer antireflection coating, a
  sixteen-layer beam splitter, a two-side-coated component carrying both, and two
  single-layer witnesses, all deposited on a Buhler Leybold Optics HELIOS 800 at Institut
  Fresnel.
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikonvr/certus-re"
license: MIT
license-url: "./LICENSE"
# The concept DOI is minted by Zenodo when the first GitHub release is published, and is not
# known before that. It is deliberately absent rather than guessed: this deposit is built on
# the principle that nothing states more than it can show, and a placeholder DOI would be the
# one piece of invented data in it. RELEASE.md carries the checklist that fills it in, here,
# in README.md section 10 and in the manuscript.
